  "releaseNotes": "Release candidate. Field settings that the scoring cannot represent are now refused instead of\n      silently corrupting results, so a value your code sets today may start throwing. Nothing stored\n      needs converting.\n      \n      - Changed: `Field.Weight`, `Field.BM25k1` and per-query field boosts reject a negative value, and\n        `Field.BM25b` rejects anything outside [0, 1], with `ArgumentOutOfRangeException`. These used to\n        be accepted and quietly wrecked the ranking: the length normalisation went negative, the stored\n        term frequency wrapped near the top of its range, and unrelated documents arrived at the maximum\n        score. If you set any of these from configuration, clamp or validate before assigning.\n      - Changed: `SetFieldConfiguration` checks the whole batch before applying any of it, so a rejected\n        call leaves the configuration untouched. An unknown field name is still reported as a return\n        value rather than an exception; only an out-of-range value throws.\n      - Fixed: a search with exactly one confirmed match reported a coverage threshold of 0, which tells\n        a caller filtering on it that everything qualifies — the opposite of what one match means.\n      - Added: `Field.SampleValue`, a short sample of the data behind each field, captured during\n        `Init()`. It is the first non-blank value found rather than the first document's, so a field that\n        is empty at the top of the file still shows what it holds. Truncated at capture.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": true,
  "title": "IndxSearchLib",
